Subject: [PATCH] allow runtime > 60 s when PANTHEON_LONG_RUN=1

Upstream hard-caps a single test run at 60 s. The thesis matrix needs one
continuous 3600 s run per scheme per direction, so the cap is lifted, but only
when the operator opts in explicitly via an environment variable. Without the
variable the behaviour is byte-for-byte upstream (cap 60 s), so an accidental
long run is impossible.

See docs/decisions/001-long-runtime.md for the cost of a 3600 s run (log volume
and analysis memory) and for the go/no-go gate.

--- a/src/experiments/arg_parser.py
+++ b/src/experiments/arg_parser.py
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+import os
 from os import path
 import sys
 import yaml
@@ -166,8 +167,13 @@ def verify_test_args(args):
             sys.exit('Cannot apply --prepend-mm-cmds, --append-mm-cmds or '
                      '--extra-mm-link-args without pantheon tunnels')
 
-    if args.runtime > 60 or args.runtime <= 0:
-        sys.exit('runtime cannot be non-positive or greater than 60 s')
+    # ccbench-remote: opt-in long runs (see patches/0001-allow-long-runtime.patch)
+    max_runtime = 60
+    if os.environ.get('PANTHEON_LONG_RUN') == '1':
+        max_runtime = 3600
+
+    if args.runtime > max_runtime or args.runtime <= 0:
+        sys.exit('runtime cannot be non-positive or greater than %d s'
+                 % max_runtime)
     if args.flows < 0:
         sys.exit('flow cannot be negative')
     if args.interval < 0:
